# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). `version` and `date-released` are
# updated by the release PR script, and the Zenodo concept DOI is added with the first
# archived release (PRD 37 §8). The repository's skill sources under skills/ are MIT.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tlilli in your work, please cite it with this metadata."
type: software
title: Tlilli
abstract: >-
  A local-first desktop editor for scientific manuscripts that turns any MCP-capable
  coding agent into a disciplined co-editor. The author writes in black ink; the agent,
  connected over the Model Context Protocol, may only propose suggestions, comments,
  verified citations and allow-listed mechanical fixes, and every sentence keeps its
  provenance.
authors:
  - name: bioedca
    website: https://github.com/bioedca
version: 0.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/bioedca/Tlilli
url: https://bioedca.github.io/Tlilli/
keywords:
  - scientific writing
  - manuscript editor
  - model context protocol
  - provenance
  - citations
  - local-first
  - tauri
  - rust
